      "text": "To find the product of the greatest common divisor (GCD) and the least common multiple (LCM) of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\), we can use the relationship between the GCD and LCM of two numbers, which is \\( \\text{GCD}(a, b) \\times \\text{LCM}(a, b) = a \\times b \\). Therefore, we first need to determine the GCD and LCM of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\).\n\nWe start by finding the prime factorizations of these numbers:\n\n\\[\n18 = 2 \\times 3^2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n42 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 7\n\\]\n\nThe GCD is the product of the lowest power of each common prime factor. The common prime factors of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\) are \\(2\\) and \\(3\\). The lowest power of \\(2\\) is \\(2^1\\) and the lowest power of \\(3\\) is \\(3^1\\). Thus, the GCD is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{GCD}(18, 42) = 2^1 \\times 3^1 = 6\n\\]\n\nNext, we find the LCM. The LCM is the product of the highest power of each prime factor. The prime factors involved are \\(2\\), \\(3\\), and \\(7\\). The highest power of \\(2\\) is \\(2^1\\), the highest power of \\(3\\) is \\(3^2\\), and the highest power of \\(7\\) is \\(7^1\\). Thus, the LCM is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(18, 42) = 2^1 \\times 3^2 \\times 7^1 = 2 \\times 9 \\times 7 = 126\n\\]\n\nNow we can find the product of the GCD and the LCM:\n\n\\[\n\\text{GCD}(18, 42) \\times \\text{LCM}(18, 42) = 6 \\times 126 = 756\n\\]\n\nSo, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{756}\\).\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Define the numbers\na = 18\nb = 42\n\n# Calculate the GCD\ngcd = math.gcd(a, b)\n\n# Calculate the LCM using the relationship LCM * GCD = a * b\nlcm = (a * b) // gcd\n\n# Calculate the product of the GCD and LCM\nproduct = gcd * lcm\nprint(product)\n```",
