      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "1. Write down the prime factorizations of $18$ and $42$:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{aligned}\n   18 &= 2 \\times 3^2, \\\\\n   42 &= 2 \\times 3 \\times 7.\n   \\end{aligned}\n   \\]\n\n2. Determine the product of the greatest common divisor (GCD) and the least common multiple (LCM) of $18$ and $42$.\n   \\[\n   \\gcd(18, 42) \\times \\text{LCM}(18, 42)\n   \\]\n   Recall that for any two integers $a$ and $b$, their product equal $a \\times b$. Hence, \n   \\[\n   \\gcd(18, 42) \\times \\text{LCM}(18, 42) = 18 \\times 42 = 756.\n   \\]\n\n3. Verify the result by calculating both GCD and LCM.\n   - For the GCD, use the prime factorizations above:\n     \\[\n     \\gcd(18, 42) = 2 \\times 3\n     \\] \n\n   - For the LCM, use the prime factorizations above:\n     \\[\n     \\text{LCM}(18, 42) = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 7 = 42.\n     \\]\n\n4. Multiply the GCD and LCM:\n   \\[\n   \\left(2 \\times 3\\right) \\times 42 = 6 \\times 42 = 756.\n   \\]\n\nConclusion: The product of the greatest common divisor and the least common multiple of $18$ and $42$ is \\(\\boxed{756}\\).",
